From 3fdb571a8abf964db59d6115a9a27cacf166bf51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:20:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: Submit Log puts the log through the whole filter,
 also before an upload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A log that Submit Log kept went through redact.sed alone, which takes
credentials and the paths of addresses out and nothing else: the
addresses of the network, MAC addresses, serial numbers, the name of the
system and of the Wi-Fi networks, and the names of films after a space
in a path stayed. And an upload went to the paste service of LibreELEC
as it was, with all of that and the keys of add-ons in it, under an
address that anyone who has it can read.

The filter is now the one of the diagnostics for logs,
/usr/lib/hades-diag/redact.sh: the identifiers become markers that stay
the same for the same value (so that a log still says which lines are
about the same device), and the credentials and the names of media go.
An upload goes through it too: the command is told to print (-c), as for
a log that is kept, what the filter prints waits in a file of /run
(in memory, readable by root only) and is handed to pastebinit, and the
file goes when that is done. A command or a filter that fails, or prints
nothing, uploads nothing, and the add-on says that the upload failed, as
it says of one that the service refuses. Whoever wants the log as it is
still has pastekodi over SSH, which is LibreELEC's command as it was.

The help of the two buttons, the text before an upload and the one after
a log is kept say what the filter does now. In es_es and es_mx these
texts address the reader as "tú", and in es_ar as "vos", as the other
texts of Hades in these files do.
